.TH ZOSEZA 1 "November 2026" "zoseza 1.3.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
zoseza \- modern eza-inspired file listing utility for IBM z/OS USS

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zoseza.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIPATH\fR ...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zoseza
is a feature-rich Python implementation inspired by the
.B eza
directory listing utility and tailored specifically for IBM z/OS UNIX System Services (USS).

It combines modern file listing capabilities with z/OS-specific features including colorized output, EBCDIC and ASCII file tag awareness, extended attribute inspection, zFS dataset resolution, and Git repository integration.

In addition to a traditional command-line interface, zoseza provides an interactive full-screen Text User Interface (TUI) for browsing, sorting, filtering, inspecting, editing, and managing files directly on the mainframe.

TUI configuration and preferences are stored in:

.RS
~/.pyeza.json
.RE

.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS

.TP
.I paths
One or more files or directories to display.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display help information and exit.

.TP
.BR -a ", " --all
Show hidden files.

.TP
.BR -l ", " --long
Display detailed file information.

.TP
.BR -g ", " --git
Display Git status information.

.TP
.BR -t ", " --time
Sort entries by modification time.

.TP
.BR -u ", " --access
Use last access time.

.TP
.BR -c ", " --ctime
Use status change time.

.TP
.BR -i ", " --icons
Display file type icons.

.TP
.B --inode
Display inode numbers.

.TP
.BR -O ", " --octal
Display permissions in octal format.

.TP
.BR -n ", " --numeric
Display numeric user and group IDs.

.TP
.BR -b ", " --blocks
Display block allocation information.

.TP
.BR -J ", " --json " " FILE
Write output in JSON format to FILE.

.TP
.BR -e ", " --ext " " EXT
Show only files matching the specified extension.

.TP
.BR -R ", " --regex " " PATTERN
Filter entries using a regular expression.

.TP
.BR -T ", " --tags
Display z/OS file tag information obtained from
.BR chtag .

.TP
.BR -x ", " --extattr
Display z/OS extended file attributes.

.TP
.B --tree
Display directories in tree format.

.TP
.BR -d ", " --directory
List directories themselves rather than their contents.

.TP
.BR -S ", " --sort-size
Sort entries by file size.

.TP
.BR -r ", " --reverse
Reverse sort order.

.TP
.BR -1 ", " --oneline
Display one entry per line.

.TP
.BR -D ", " --dsn
Show underlying zFS dataset names.

.TP
.BI --color " {auto|always|never}"
Control colorized output.

.TP
.B --no-color
Disable all terminal colors.

.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Display version information and exit.

.TP
.B --tui
Launch the interactive Text User Interface.

.SH FILES

.TP
.I ~/.pyeza.json
User preferences and TUI configuration file.

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
List files in the current directory:
.B zoseza.py

.TP
Show hidden files with long output:
.B zoseza.py -al

.TP
Display Git status information:
.B zoseza.py -g

.TP
Show file tags and extended attributes:
.B zoseza.py -T -x

.TP
Display a directory tree:
.B zoseza.py --tree

.TP
Launch the TUI:
.B zoseza.py --tui

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR ls (1),
.BR eza (1),
.BR chtag (1),
.BR extattr (1)

.SH AUTHOR

zoseza was developed for IBM z/OS UNIX System Services users seeking a modern, feature-rich alternative to traditional file listing tools.

